<title>FRANCE: Second Ariane-5 shot set for early July 1997.</title>
<headline>Second Ariane-5 shot set for early July 1997.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>A second attempt to launch Europe's new Ariane-5 space rocket successfully will be made early next July, the European and French space agencies said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Ariane-5's maiden flight in June ended in disaster when ground control blew up the rocket shortly after take-off from Kourou, in French Guiana on the northeast coast of South America, when it veered off course.</p>
<p>A statement by the European Space Agency (ESA) and France's CNES national space agency said a third test was scheduled for November 1997.</p>
</text>
